3. SCOPE: WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

3.1 Covered. This license applies to the original contents of this repository,
    namely:

    (a) `src/` — the TypeScript source of the VOLDBASE domain, application,
        infrastructure and public module surface;
    (b) `bin/` — the command-line entry point;
    (c) `tests/` — the test suites;
    (d) `docs/` — architecture, decision records and security documentation,
        except any file that carries its own copyright or license statement;
    (e) the original text of `README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `NOTICE`,
        `TRADEMARKS.md`, this license, and the repository configuration files
        (`package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `tsconfig.json`,
        `tsconfig.build.json`, `.editorconfig`, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`,
        and `.github/`).

3.2 Excluded — third-party components. This license does NOT apply to any
    third-party software, package, type definition or other material, whether
    vendored in this repository or installed as a dependency. Those components
    remain governed by their own licenses and their own copyright holders. See
    `NOTICE` for the components this repository currently depends on. Nothing
    in this license claims ownership of, or grants rights in, third-party code.

3.3 Excluded — contributors' work. This license does NOT transfer or claim
    ownership of any contribution made by anyone other than the Copyright
    Holder. A contributor, or the person or organisation that holds the
    copyright in the contribution, retains that copyright and licenses the
    contribution as described in section 8. Nothing in this license should be
    read as an assignment of a contributor's copyright.

3.4 Excluded — names, logos and brand identity. This license grants no rights
    in the VOLDBASE name, logo, wordmark, visual identity or any other
    trademark or brand element. See `TRADEMARKS.md`.

3.5 Excluded — files with their own terms. If a file in this repository carries
    an explicit copyright or license header, that file is governed by that
    header, and this license does not override it.

3.6 Not retroactive: earlier versions and prior grants. This license applies to
    the contents of this repository as distributed under this license, from the
    commit that first includes it onward. It does not apply retroactively, and
    it does not revoke, cancel, narrow, withdraw or replace any permission that
    was already granted under a previous license for a version, release or copy
    distributed under that previous license. In particular:

    (a) A version distributed under the MIT License remains available under the
        MIT License for anyone who obtained it under that license. This draft
        does not claim that those permissions ended when it was published.
    (b) Rights already exercised are not made retroactively unlicensed, and no
        past use is recharacterised by this draft.
    (c) A copy obtained under an earlier license continues to be governed by
        that earlier license; a copy obtained under this license is governed by
        this license.
    (d) Verified boundary, prior side. The MIT License applied to every commit
        on the `main` branch from the initial commit `5aee287` (2026-11-14)
        through commit `1768aad` (2026-11-18) inclusive. `LICENSE` was not
        modified between those two commits: the MIT text in the initial commit
        and the text in `1768aad` are the same file. This draft does not apply
        to any of those commits, and it does not apply to any copy obtained
        from them.
    (e) Start of this license. This draft applies to repository contents
        from the first commit on `main` whose tree contains it. That commit
        is identified by that fact alone, not by its commit message or by
        the way the change was landed: whether it is a merge commit, a
        squashed commit or a direct commit, the boundary is the first commit
        on `main` that contains this draft. The first such commit is
        `2b31d97589d5af7b4c7e7925b725e7bd53c1c2e9`, and this draft applies
        from it onward.
    (f) No releases. The repository has no tags and no published releases, so
        the boundary is commit-based only: there are no release artifacts on
        either side of it.

    This section records the Copyright Holder's intent not to revoke prior
    grants. It does not decide the legal effect of a license change on any
    particular distribution. Copies taken from an unmerged branch that carries
    this draft are not releases, and they carry the draft text rather than a
    final license; that label does not by itself determine what legal effect, if
    any, the draft has on such a copy. That question, the labelling of a product
    or repository that contains files under both licenses, and whether any copy
    of an earlier version was distributed outside this repository, remain
    unresolved and are recorded in `NOTICE` ("Prior licensing") and ADR-0020.

