    (c) Not the modifier's work. A recipient of a modified version receives the
        Copyright Holder's permission in the Software. The modifier's own
        original additions are not licensed by the Copyright Holder and are
        available only on whatever terms the modifier grants; if the modifier
        grants none, this license gives the recipient no right to use them.

    This direct-grant construction states the Copyright Holder's intent. Whether
    it is effective in a given jurisdiction, and whether a recipient's
    permission survives a redistributor's breach in every legal system, are
    questions for qualified counsel and are recorded in `NOTICE` ("Open
    questions for legal review"). This draft does not present the construction
    as a legal conclusion.

