14. GENERAL

14.1 No waiver. A failure or delay in enforcing a term is not a waiver of that
     term or of any other term.

14.2 Severability. If a provision is held invalid or unenforceable, it is
     modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable, and the
     remaining provisions stay in force.

14.3 No assignment. You may not assign or transfer this license or its
     permissions without the Copyright Holder's prior written consent. The
     Copyright Holder may assign the copyright and this license.

14.4 Document hierarchy and entire agreement. The documents that make up this
     licensing documentation have separate and limited roles:

     (a) `LICENSE` (this document) governs the permissions in the Software, and
         it is the only one of these documents that grants or limits those
         permissions;
     (b) `TRADEMARKS.md` governs use of the Brand and any trademark right. It
         grants no permission in the Software;
     (c) `NOTICE` provides copyright notices, attribution, third-party
         disclosures and factual statements about the current state of the
         Software. It grants no permission in the Software.

     Where `NOTICE` or `TRADEMARKS.md` appears to state a permission or a
     restriction in the Software that differs from this license, this license
     governs and the other document does not override it. A separate written
     permission under section 5 governs where it applies. Together these
     documents replace any earlier statement about licensing the Software,
     except rights already granted for copies obtained under a previous license
     (section 3.6).

14.5 Governing law and venue. NOT DESIGNATED IN THIS DRAFT. The governing law,
     jurisdiction and dispute-resolution forum are unresolved and must be
     chosen with legal advice before this draft is treated as final. Nothing in
     this draft should be read as choosing them by implication.

14.6 Language. This license is written in English. A translation is for
     convenience only; the English text expresses the Copyright Holder's intent.

